Description: CVE-2026-44690 - Cross-zone wildcard cache poisoning via RRSIG.labels manipulation
 A malicious authoritative server could poison the RRset cache of a
 validating resolver with wildcard-expanded records for names outside
 the authority of the RRSIG signer, by manipulating the RRSIG labels
 field. This fix:
  * Rejects RRSIGs whose label count is lower than the signer name's
    label count (dnskey_verify_rrset_sig in val_sigcrypt.c).
  * When caching a wildcard-expanded RRset, verifies that the derived
    canonical parent name falls within the authority of every RRSIG
    signer (dname_subdomain_rrsig_signers in services/cache/rrset.c).
  * Postpones the aggressive-NSEC wildcard cache update in
    validate_positive_response until the wildcard proof has actually
    succeeded, so bogus responses can no longer populate the cache.
 The helper rrsig_get_signer is exported from val_utils for reuse by
 the rrset cache.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/f7637a4f1811f4a9331707d8a95cf0af65a97c0f
Author: W.C.A. Wijngaards <wouter@nlnetlabs.nl>
Last-Update: 2026-07-28
