Description: CVE-2026-55973 - dns-error-reporting stack buffer overflow
 A stack buffer overflow can be triggered via the RFC9567 "DNS Error
 Reporting" feature ('dns-error-reporting: yes') when a malformed agent
 domain name is processed. The upstream fix (commit 96f8755) hardens
 find_closest_of_type() in services/cache/dns.c so its label-snipping
 loop stops on a zero-length label instead of walking past the end of
 the name, and reworks dns_error_reporting() in services/mesh.c to bound
 the agent domain length by dname_valid().
 .
 The RFC9567 DNS Error Reporting feature (dns_error_reporting(),
 LDNS_EDNS_REPORT_CHANNEL, agent_domain) was introduced upstream in
 release 1.23.0 and is entirely absent from this target
 (unbound 1.22.0-2+deb13u3, which predates the affected range
 1.23.0-1.25.1). The services/mesh.c hunk therefore has no code to
 attach to on this version and is omitted. This patch applies the
 defensive find_closest_of_type() label-length guard from the upstream
 fix, which does textually apply here, as conservative hardening of the
 shared label-snipping loop.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/NLnetLabs/unbound/commit/96f875552023c0ccf376ebe050519f12f3371dc9
Author: W.C.A. Wijngaards <wouter@nlnetlabs.nl>
Bug: CVE-2026-55973
Last-Update: 2026-08-01
---
--- a/services/cache/dns.c
+++ b/services/cache/dns.c
@@ -259,6 +259,8 @@ find_closest_of_type(struct module_env*

 		/* snip off front label */
 		lablen = *qname;
+		if(lablen == 0)
+			break;
 		qname += lablen + 1;
 		qnamelen -= lablen + 1;
 	}
Description: CVE-2026-50252 - Possible cache poisoning attack by mapping source port population per thread.
 Unbound shared a single population of source ports across all worker
 threads, which reduced the entropy of the (source port, query ID) tuple
 available to an off-path attacker and made cache poisoning attacks more
 feasible. This patch introduces a shared_ports structure that maps the
 source port population per thread, restoring the intended per-thread port
 randomisation. It also folds in the follow-up commits that guard access to
 the shared ports interface array during initialisation/thread setup, fix a
 sign-of-comparison warning, and fix unused-variable warnings when compiled
 without threads.
 .
 Includes the upstream regression test additions in testcode/unittcpreuse.c.
